        "original_id": "a66c6f43-6541-58d4-aba9-7f06f4071aae",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sarah Jacobson, Arthur Hiller, John Fusco\n- Films: I Was a Teenage Serial Killer, The Babe\n- Places: Norwalk, Connecticut, New York City, United States\n- Roles: independent filmmaker, director, writer, producer\n\nFacts:\n- Sarah Jacobson was born on August 25, 1971, in Norwalk, Connecticut.\n- Arthur Hiller was born on November 22, 1923, and became a Canadian-American television and film director.\n- Arthur Hiller directed more than 33 films during a 50-year career.\n- The film The Babe was directed by Arthur Hiller, written by John Fusco, and released in the United States on April 17, 1992.\n- Sarah Jacobson wrote, produced, and filmed her own movies as an independent filmmaker.\n- Sarah Jacobson wrote and directed the underground no-budget film I Was a Teenage Serial Killer.\n- Sarah Jacobson died on February 13, 2004, in New York City.\n- Arthur Hiller died on August 17, 2016.",
